e": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}], "template_override": 1}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally in the UK"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Buckingham Palace"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Exploring Ancient Sites > Stonehenge"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about directions to places in  a limited range of social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "How Far Is It?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The question \"How far is it?\" asks for the distance from where you are to another place.  You use the Simple Present tense to ask this question. <br/><br/>You can use <span class=\"strong\">near</span>, <span class=\"strong\">close</span> and<span class=\"strong\"> far</span> to say the distance of something to where you are. <br><br><span class=\"italic\">Near</span> and <span class=\"italic\">close</span> have the same meaning. Far has the opposite meaning.<br><br>The expression <span class=\"italic\">too far</span> means something is very far in a negative way.<br><br>You often talk about how far something is using the time it takes to walk or drive.  A hyphen ( - ) goes between the number and the word <span class=\"italic\">minute</span> or <span class=\"italic\">hour</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "How far is it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's about 10 miles away."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's about 40-minute walk."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's too far to walk."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The Underground is close."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Imperatives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Imperatives are verbs in the base form.  You don't use a subject. <br><br>You can use Imperatives when you give directions or suggestions."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Directions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Suggestions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Take the Tube to James Park station.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Visit the Queen's Gallery and Royal Mews.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Walk through St. James Park.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Contact the visitors' office for an application form.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Make a left at the corner of Victoria.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Look at the beautiful palace! </span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "visitors' office"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place where tourists get information about a specific place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Contact the visitors' office for an application form."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear at a visitor's office."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "weather"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the temperature and other outside conditions (such as rain, cloudiness, etc.) at a particular time and place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How do you like the London weather?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "damp"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cold and wet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's pretty damp in London."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cloudy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "ready to rain; many clouds are in the sky"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: London is often cool and cloudy.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "not so much"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not a lot"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Agent: How do you like the London weather?  Sally: Well ... not so much."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Royal Mews"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a street beside Buckingham Palace"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Visit the Queen's Gallery and Royal Mews. They're beautiful."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le08ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online to find information about Buckingham Palace."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Complete the table."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Summarize the information in 4 - 5 sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present the information to your class."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Answer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When was Buckingham Palace built?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Who built it?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Who lived there?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What can visitors see?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When is it open?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "te